[ti:Day 21]

[00:00.00]decline [dɪˈklaɪn]vi. 下降；衰落 vt. 谢绝 n. 下降；衰退； 谢绝 例 The size and number of transactions showed a more than 30 percent decline last year. 搭 decline to 降低至 / on the decline 在减少 中；在衰退中
[00:17.52]expansion [ɪkˈspænʃn]n. 膨胀；扩张；发展 例 Expansion of domestic demand is really reasonable as China has such a big market.
[00:29.40]prorate [prəʊˈreɪt]v. 〈美〉按比例分配；摊派 例 It is usual that the seller and the buyer should prorate the taxes in the sale of real estate.
[00:42.36]tie-up [ˈtaɪʌp]n. 联合；联系；企业协作 搭 tie-up between...and... …与…之间的协作
[00:49.20]element [ˈelɪmənt]n. (基本)物质，要素；成分；元 件；[pl.] 基础，原理；自然力 例 He is a very serious guy, out of elements of gossip. 搭 in sb.'s element 内行 / out of sb.'s element 外行
[01:04.68]kickback [ˈkɪkbæk]n. 回扣，佣金；强烈反应 例 He got a lot of kickbacks in this big project.
[01:12.72]testimony [ˈtestɪməni]n. (法庭上证人的)证词；证明；证据 搭 bear testimony 证明 / produce testimony of 提出…的证据
[01:22.32]template [ˈtempleɪt]n. 模板 搭 template for …的模板
[01:27.00]hive [haɪv]n. 热闹场所 vt. 积蓄 例 The little girl, standing there silently, seemed that she had never seen such a hive of industry. 搭 hive off 从团体中分出
[01:41.04]add-on [ˈædɒn]n. 计算机附件；附加物，附属品 例 A loyalty card is just considered a useful add-on for many hotel users.
[01:51.60]scanner [ˈskænə(r)]n. 扫描器，扫描仪
[01:54.84]preoccupation [priˌɒkjuˈpeɪʃn]n. 抢先占有；全神贯注；使人全 神贯注的事物；当务之急 例 Ensuring the supply of natural resources has become a major preoccupation for the government.
[02:11.16]recipient [rɪˈsɪpiənt]n. 接受者；接收方
[02:14.76]inconsiderate [ˌɪnkənˈsɪdərət]a. 轻率的；不顾及别人的；考虑 不周的 例 He's often inconsiderate to his colleagues.
[02:25.08]luxury [ˈlʌkʃəri]a. 奢侈的 n. 奢侈品；享受
[02:28.56]incentive [ɪnˈsentɪv]n. 动机；刺激；激励；奖励 a. 激励的 例 With more supply in the market, there's more incentive to sell.
[02:39.60]stub [stʌb]n. 票据存根，票根
[02:41.88]underutilise [ˌʌndəˈjuːtəlaɪz]vt. 未充分使用
[02:46.32]flourish [ˈflʌrɪʃ]vi. 繁荣，兴旺；成功；盛行 n. 繁荣，兴 旺；成功；全盛期 例 If the United States wants to see democracy flourish it cannot close its markets.
[03:00.00]imminent [ˈɪmɪnənt]a. 迫近的；即将来临或发生的 例 He told us not to act until the threat is imminent.
[03:08.88]crunch [kr ʌnt ʃ ]v i. 嘎吱嘎吱地咀嚼；摩擦 n. 〈口〉 关键时刻；经济紧缩；不足，短缺 例 People who crunch nuts at the movies can be very annoying. 搭 when it comes to the crunch 当关键时刻到 来时
[03:24.12]reverse [rɪˈvɜːs]a. 相反的，反向的；反面的；颠倒的 v. 颠倒；倒转
[03:28.92]jot [dʒɒt]n. (通常用否定结构)一点儿；(最)小额； (最)少量 vi. 匆匆记下 例 Every year the award ceremony seems that not a jot has changed. 搭 jot down 草草记下，匆匆记下 / not care a jot 毫不在乎 / not one jot or little 一点儿也没有
[03:47.16]nosedive [ˈnəʊzdaɪv]n./vi. (价格等的)猛跌；(飞机的)俯 冲；(情况)突然变坏 例 It is the second-largest drop of the company's profits following a 30 percent nosedive last year.
[04:03.12]privatise [ˈpraɪvətaɪz]vt. 使私有化 例 He doesn't plan to privatise the company.
[04:10.92]behemoth [bɪˈhiːmɒθ]n. 巨兽；庞然大物 例 Google, an important search engine on the Web, is also a global behemoth.
[04:21.72]pertinent [ˈpɜːtɪnənt]a. 有关的；中肯的；切题的 例 This is the data pertinent to the design of new products.
[04:31.56]stonewalling [ˌstəʊnˈwɔːlɪŋ]n. 石墙；妨碍(或阻碍)议程
[04:36.48]bilateral [ˌbaɪˈlætərəl]a. 两边的；双边的，双向作用的 例 To date, many western countries have bilateral agreements with China.
[04:48.36]resort [rɪˈzɔːt]vi. 求助；诉诸 n. 求助，求助的人；手 段；度假胜地 搭 as a last resort 万不得已(作为最后手段) / resort to 求助于；诉诸
[04:58.08]delinquency [dɪˈlɪŋkwənsi]n. 失职；失职罪；失约；拖欠的债 务(税款)
[05:03.60]favourable [ˈfeɪvərəbl]a. 有利的；优惠的；赞成的，肯定的 例 Malta's major resources are limestone, a favourable geographic location, and a productive labour force. 搭 be favourable to 赞成 / make a favourable impression on sb. 给某人留下良好的印象
[05:26.16]oversee [ˌəʊvəˈsiː]vt. 俯瞰；监督 例 Amy was appointed to oversee the execution of the entire project.
[05:36.00]curtail [kɜːˈteɪl]vt. 缩短；削减；剥夺(某人的)特权 例 Job losses have rised to its highest level in recent years as banks curtail credit to small businesses.
[05:50.64]beforehand [bɪˈfɔːhænd]ad. 预先，事先；提前地；超前地 a. 预先的；早作准备的 例 The offsetting purchase occurs any time within 30 days beforehand or afterwards and the loss can't be deducted. 搭 be beforehand with 预先准备好 / beforehand alarm 预警 / beforehand process 预加工
[06:15.24]authority [ɔːˈθɒrəti]n. 权威；职权，权限；权力；证 据；[pl.] 官方；行政管理机关 例 The regulation stipulates responsibilities on the part of sellers for the repair, replacement and refund of private cars manufactured and sold in China. 搭 have authority over 有权；管理
[06:39.84]minority [maɪˈnɒrəti]n. 少数；少数派；未成年；少数民族 搭 in a/the minority 处于少数的
[06:46.80]application [ˌæplɪˈkeɪʃn]n. 应用；实施；适用性；请求，申 请 例 The persuasiveness of advertisement is decided by the application of language. 搭 make an application to sb. for help 请求某 人帮助
[07:04.32]studio [ˈstjuːdiəʊ]n. 播音室；录音室；工作室；电影摄 影棚；制片厂 搭 photographic studio 摄影室
[07:11.88]channel [ˈtʃænl] n. [常pl.]渠道；频道；沟渠，海峡；水 道，航道 vt. 输送；引导 搭 channel sth. into/through sth. 把...导入...； 把…纳入…
[07:22.80]annum [ˈænəm]n. 年，岁 例 The lawyer can earn $200,000 per annum. 搭 per annum 每年
[07:30.24]embarrassing [ɪmˈbærəsɪŋ]a. 令人为难的，尴尬的 例 It's extremely embarrassing to be blacklisted by the banking system.
